      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that `withValueNulls(Nulls, Nulls)` correctly sets both value-nulls and content-nulls on a `JsonSetter.Value` built from a mock annotation with null fields. Let me write the improved version.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test adds a descriptive method name (`test_withValueNulls_setsBothNullStrategiesToAsEmpty`), a Javadoc comment explaining the intent, and more readable variable names (`mockAnnotation`, `baseValue`, `asEmpty`, `updatedValue`) — all while preserving the exact same calls and assertions as the original."
